<section id="live-search" class="rf-live-search" data-seattle-search>
    <p class="v2-eyebrow">Search public records here</p><h2>Seattle residential tank lookup.</h2>
    <p>Search the City's published residential decommissioning records, beginning in 1996. This is a dataset search—not a search of every Fire file, a commercial tank register or a tank-free certificate.</p>
    <form data-seattle-form hidden aria-describedby="seattle-privacy seattle-scope">
        <div class="rf-fields"><label for="seattle-house">House number<input id="seattle-house" name="house" required maxlength="7" pattern="[0-9]{1,6}[A-Za-z]?" autocomplete="off" placeholder="House number only"></label><label for="seattle-street">Street name / number<input id="seattle-street" name="street" required minlength="2" maxlength="60" autocomplete="off" placeholder="For example: Main or 15th"></label></div>
        <p id="seattle-scope" class="rf-caption">Use the street's distinctive name or number, not the full address, unit or ZIP. Direction and suffix abbreviations can differ. Confirm every candidate against the subject property.</p>
        <p id="seattle-privacy" class="rf-caption">Only pressing Search sends these terms directly to Seattle Open Data. Oil Tank Route does not receive or save the terms or results. Seattle's provider can log its requests. Nothing is submitted to an agency records desk or added to your worksheet.</p>
        <div class="rf-actions"><button type="submit">Search Seattle dataset</button><button type="reset">Clear search &amp; results</button></div>
    </form>
    <noscript><p>Direct lookup needs JavaScript. Use the official dataset link below; the rest of this record guide works without JavaScript.</p></noscript>
    <p data-seattle-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    <div data-seattle-results></div>
    <p><a href="https://data.seattle.gov/Built-Environment/Underground-Storage-Tank-UST-Records-Residential/xvj2-ai6y" rel="external">Source: City of Seattle residential UST dataset ↗</a> · <a href="#request-plan">Need the underlying report? Prepare a records request ↓</a></p>
    <p class="rf-caption">No result does not establish that no tank exists. An issue date is not completion. Missing tank details may mean the City has not received the required follow-up report. Older, differently addressed or unpublished records need separate follow-up.</p>
</section>
